{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794535048648,"sessionID":"ses_e2d61a4abffeh9vQudGvgT5Z1T","part":{"id":"prt_1d29fc5c8001qUcCiO5cEpkzFf","sessionID":"ses_e2d61a4abffeh9vQudGvgT5Z1T","messageID":"msg_1d29fb9d60014A6hMouexdEW5J","type":"step-start","snapshot":"26f9402bc7f92e125b718bb787f6ba210c9a64a8"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794535057732,"sessionID":"ses_e2d61a4abffeh9vQudGvgT5Z1T","part":{"partID":"prt_1d29fe69e001qb6lAghJ3uRayI","sessionID":"ses_e2d61a4abffeh9vQudGvgT5Z1T","messageID":"msg_1d29fb9d60014A6hMouexdEW5J","type":"tool","id":"call_6211ae5d260e433d937d8f6b","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && git -c core.fsmonitor=false log -p -3 -- .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/scoring-compatibility.json | head -160"},"output":"commit a57ce61a1345334a9cf2a520124d7bf896f297ea\nAuthor: Michel Kerkmeester <82775228+MichelKerkmeester@users.noreply.github.com>\nDate:   Fri Nov 13 01:58:41 2026 +0100\n\n    feat(system-skill-advisor): put the command and policy in the brief and record offers\n    \n    A surfaced command reached the model as an internal id such as\n    command-spec-kit-plan, so the model could not tell which slash command\n    to start or whether it had to ask first. A recommendation now carries\n    kind, command, policy and ownerSkillId, filled from one generated\n    command table, and the hook brief prints them in its head, for example\n    \"use sk-doc -> /create:readme (start)\". A hub that gets a command from\n    its compiled route carries the policy too.\n    \n    When the daemon is down the CLI fallback shows a command only when the\n    prompt typed it, and otherwise names the owner skill. The four old\n    spec-kit command ids are renamed to command-speckit-*, the dead Python\n    /prompt row and the allow-list are gone, and the doctor command strings\n    come from the same generated table.\n    \n    The router reach check counts a command row as a hit for its owner hub,\n    which makes it pass with real embeddings. A plain request to fix a typo\n    in a guide now routes to sk-doc. Two floored candidates cluster on their\n    score margin, which removes the last same-owner ambiguity on a typed\n    command.\n    \n    The Python fallback keeps its four compatibility rows under the new ids.\n    Deleting them cost it one labeled row, and keeping them leaves it one\n    row better than before. Pinned numbers hold: typed recall 24 of 44,\n    false offers 0 of 35, scorer baseline 159, 50, 20 and 5. The advisor\n    suite passes with 1513 tests.\n    \n    Reachability and attribution, from the research on the before arm:\n    \n    The before arm showed that a start rate alone says little: Codex got no\n    advisor brief in any of its 24 sessions because a fresh clone has no\n    approved project hooks, and DSH got none because the runner marked its\n    turns as fan-out leaves. Neither fact was visible in the run log.\n    \n    The runner now records on every line which command and policy the\n    advisor offered for that prompt in that checkout and whether the brief\n    was delivered, and a backfill mode adds the same fields to a finished\n    log. It no longer passes the lineage patch to DSH. The scorer reports\n    offered rows and starts among them, capped start rows apart, start and\n    write counts per policy and an incomplete arm, and it resolves an argued\n    doctor route such as /doctor:git hooks to its command document.\n    \n    Two read-only doctor checks are new: one says whether the checkout's\n    Codex advisor hook is approved, called from /doctor:runtime-mirrors, and\n    one names each runtime whose prompt hook is missing in a target\n    repository, called from /doctor:symlink check. The install guide gains\n    the Codex approval step and DSH. The DSH guard bundle keeps the prompt\n    advisor on unless its row says false.\n    \n    A true cold first prompt was measured at 611 to 844 ms with a live\n    brief, so the planned session-start warm-up is dropped.\n    \n    Spec: system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build\n    Commit-Id: 0013733\n\ndiff --git a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/scoring-compatibility.json b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/scoring-compatibility.json\nindex 7319e4ee7c..95094eca4e 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/scoring-compatibility.json\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/scoring-compatibility.json\n@@ -265,9 +265,9 @@\n   ],\n   \"python\": [\n     {\n-      \"inventoryId\": \"command-spec-kit-plan\",\n+      \"inventoryId\": \"command-speckit-plan\",\n       \"order\": 0,\n-      \"id\": \"command-spec-kit-plan\",\n+      \"id\": \"command-speckit-plan\",\n       \"description\": \"Run the SpecKit 8-step planning workflow using /speckit:plan.\",\n       \"slashMarkers\": [\n         \"/speckit:plan\",\n@@ -276,9 +276,9 @@\n       \"owningSkill\": \"system-spec-kit\"\n     },\n     {\n-      \"inventoryId\": \"command-spec-kit-complete\",\n+      \"inventoryId\": \"command-speckit-complete\",\n       \"order\": 1,\n-      \"id\": \"command-spec-kit-complete\",\n+      \"id\": \"command-speckit-complete\",\n       \"description\": \"Run the full SpecKit 14+ step lifecycle using /speckit:complete.\",\n       \"slashMarkers\": [\n         \"/speckit:complete\",\n@@ -287,9 +287,9 @@\n       \"owningSkill\": \"system-spec-kit\"\n     },\n     {\n-      \"inventoryId\": \"command-spec-kit-implement\",\n+      \"inventoryId\": \"command-speckit-implement\",\n       \"order\": 2,\n-      \"id\": \"command-spec-kit-implement\",\n+      \"id\": \"command-speckit-implement\",\n       \"description\": \"Run the SpecKit 9-step implementation workflow using /speckit:implement.\",\n       \"slashMarkers\": [\n         \"/speckit:implement\",\n@@ -320,9 +320,9 @@\n       \"owningSkill\": \"deep-review\"\n     },\n     {\n-      \"inventoryId\": \"command-spec-kit-resume\",\n+      \"inventoryId\": \"command-speckit-resume\",\n       \"order\": 5,\n-      \"id\": \"command-spec-kit-resume\",\n+      \"id\": \"command-speckit-resume\",\n       \"description\": \"Resume an existing spec folder using /speckit:resume.\",\n       \"slashMarkers\": [\n         \"/speckit:resume\",\n@@ -605,7 +605,7 @@\n   \"pythonOwnerNormalization\": {\n     \"command-create-agent\": \"create:agent\",\n     \"command-create-manual-testing-playbook\": \"create:manual-testing-playbook\",\n-    \"command-spec-kit-resume\": \"system-spec-kit\",\n+    \"command-speckit-resume\": \"system-spec-kit\",\n     \"command-spec-kit-deep-research\": \"deep-research\",\n     \"command-spec-kit-deep-review\": \"deep-review\"\n   }\n\ncommit 2389b84f7ef7e0d3a9acd69d8ad866dc050b22ca\nAuthor: Michel Kerkmeester <82775228+MichelKerkmeester@users.noreply.github.com>\nDate:   Thu Nov 12 18:55:23 2026 +0100\n\n    feat(system-skill-advisor): attach hub commands and give each command its own row\n    \n    A hub recommendation now carries the slash command of its single routed\n    mode, taken from a table generated from the hubs' own mode registries.\n    A deep-loop command is attached only when the prompt asks for that\n    effort, and a hub stays silent when the command's own row already ranks\n    in the same result. Every /speckit command and /prompt:improve has its\n    own advisor row that passes only on its own phrase or slash string, and\n    a command row and its owner skill no longer count as an ambiguous tie.\n    \n    The umbrella ids command-spec-kit, memory:save, command-memory-save and\n    command-prompt-improver are retired for one id per command. Gold lines,\n    fixtures, both baselines and the Python scorer are re-pointed, and\n    AGENTS.md Gate 4, the root README, the orchestrate agent with its\n    runtime mirrors and the doctor manifest name the deep-loop command rows\n    in their place.\n    \n    The hook asks for the compiled route of the top recommendation only,\n    through the new compiledRouteTopOnly option. /create:changelog now asks\n    first because its release path pushes a tag and publishes a release.\n    Standalone skills may carry command-metadata.json.\n    \n    Component changelog entries, READMEs, the feature catalog, one playbook\n    scenario and the v4.0.2.1 release notes describe the change. Phase 003\n    stays In Progress: plain-chat holdout reach is still 0 of 44.\n    \n    Spec: system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/003-plain-chat-command-reach\n    Commit-Id: 0013668\n\ndiff --git a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/scoring-compatibility.json b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/scoring-compatibility.json\nindex 7bc5f183ca..7319e4ee7c 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/scoring-compatibility.json\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/scoring-compatibility.json\n@@ -1,73 +1,6 @@\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"commit a57ce61a1345334a9cf2a520124d7bf896f297ea\nAuthor: Michel Kerkmeester <82775228+MichelKerkmeester@users.noreply.github.com>\nDate:   Fri Nov 13 01:58:41 2026 +0100\n\n    feat(system-skill-advisor): put the command and policy in the brief and record offers\n    \n    A surfaced command reached the model as an internal id such as\n    command-spec-kit-plan, so the model could not tell which slash command\n    to start or whether it had to ask first. A recommendation now carries\n    kind, command, policy and ownerSkillId, filled from one generated\n    command table, and the hook brief prints them in its head, for example\n    \"use sk-doc -> /create:readme (start)\". A hub that gets a command from\n    its compiled route carries the policy too.\n    \n    When the daemon is down the CLI fallback shows a command only when the\n    prompt typed it, and otherwise names the owner skill. The four old\n    spec-kit command ids are renamed to command-speckit-*, the dead Python\n    /prompt row and the allow-list are gone, and the doctor command strings\n    come from the same generated table.\n    \n    The router reach check counts a command row as a hit for its owner hub,\n    which makes it pass with real embeddings. A plain request to fix a typo\n    in a guide now routes to sk-doc. Two floored candidates cluster on their\n    score margin, which removes the last same-owner ambiguity on a typed\n    command.\n    \n    The Python fallback keeps its four compatibility rows under the new ids.\n    Deleting them cost it one labeled row, and keeping them leaves it one\n    row better than before. Pinned numbers hold: typed recall 24 of 44,\n    false offers 0 of 35, scorer baseline 159, 50, 20 and 5. The advisor\n    suite passes with 1513 tests.\n    \n    Reachability and attribution, from the research on the before arm:\n    \n    The before arm showed that a start rate alone says little: Codex got no\n    advisor brief in any of its 24 sessions because a fresh clone has no\n    approved project hooks, and DSH got none because the runner marked its\n    turns as fan-out leaves. Neither fact was visible in the run log.\n    \n    The runner now records on every line which command and policy the\n    advisor offered for that prompt in that checkout and whether the brief\n    was delivered, and a backfill mode adds the same fields to a finished\n    log. It no longer passes the lineage patch to DSH. The scorer reports\n    offered rows and starts among them, capped start rows apart, start and\n    write counts per policy and an incomplete arm, and it resolves an argued\n    doctor route such as /doctor:git hooks to its command document.\n    \n    Two read-only doctor checks are new: one says whether the checkout's\n    Codex advisor hook is approved, called from /doctor:runtime-mirrors, and\n    one names each runtime whose prompt hook is missing in a target\n    repository, called from /doctor:symlink check. The install guide gains\n    the Codex approval step and DSH. The DSH guard bundle keeps the prompt\n    advisor on unless its row says false.\n    \n    A true cold first prompt was measured at 611 to 844 ms with a live\n    brief, so the planned session-start warm-up is dropped.\n    \n    Spec: system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build\n    Commit-Id: 0013733\n\ndiff --git a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/scoring-compatibility.json b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/scoring-compatibility.json\nindex 7319e4ee7c..95094eca4e 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/scoring-compatibility.json\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/scoring-compatibility.json\n@@ -265,9 +265,9 @@\n   ],\n   \"python\": [\n     {\n-      \"inventoryId\": \"command-spec-kit-plan\",\n+      \"inventoryId\": \"command-speckit-plan\",\n       \"order\": 0,\n-      \"id\": \"command-spec-kit-plan\",\n+      \"id\": \"command-speckit-plan\",\n       \"description\": \"Run the SpecKit 8-step planning workflow using /speckit:plan.\",\n       \"slashMarkers\": [\n         \"/speckit:plan\",\n@@ -276,9 +276,9 @@\n       \"owningSkill\": \"system-spec-kit\"\n     },\n     {\n-      \"inventoryId\": \"command-spec-kit-complete\",\n+      \"inventoryId\": \"command-speckit-complete\",\n       \"order\": 1,\n-      \"id\": \"command-spec-kit-complete\",\n+      \"id\": \"command-speckit-complete\",\n       \"description\": \"Run the full SpecKit 14+ step lifecycle using /speckit:complete.\",\n       \"slashMarkers\": [\n         \"/speckit:complete\",\n@@ -287,9 +287,9 @@\n       \"owningSkill\": \"system-spec-kit\"\n     },\n     {\n-      \"inventoryId\": \"command-spec-kit-implement\",\n+      \"inventoryId\": \"command-speckit-implement\",\n       \"order\": 2,\n-      \"id\": \"command-spec-kit-implement\",\n+      \"id\": \"command-speckit-implement\",\n       \"description\": \"Run the SpecKit 9-step implementation workflow using /speckit:implement.\",\n       \"slashMarkers\": [\n         \"/speckit:implement\",\n@@ -320,9 +320,9 @@\n       \"owningSkill\": \"deep-review\"\n     },\n     {\n-      \"inventoryId\": \"command-spec-kit-resume\",\n+      \"inventoryId\": \"command-speckit-resume\",\n       \"order\": 5,\n-      \"id\": \"command-spec-kit-resume\",\n+      \"id\": \"command-speckit-resume\",\n       \"description\": \"Resume an existing spec folder using /speckit:resume.\",\n       \"slashMarkers\": [\n         \"/speckit:resume\",\n@@ -605,7 +605,7 @@\n   \"pythonOwnerNormalization\": {\n     \"command-create-agent\": \"create:agent\",\n     \"command-create-manual-testing-playbook\": \"create:manual-testing-playbook\",\n-    \"command-spec-kit-resume\": \"system-spec-kit\",\n+    \"command-speckit-resume\": \"system-spec-kit\",\n     \"command-spec-kit-deep-research\": \"deep-research\",\n     \"command-spec-kit-deep-review\": \"deep-review\"\n   }\n\ncommit 2389b84f7ef7e0d3a9acd69d8ad866dc050b22ca\nAuthor: Michel Kerkmeester <82775228+MichelKerkmeester@users.noreply.github.com>\nDate:   Thu Nov 12 18:55:23 2026 +0100\n\n    feat(system-skill-advisor): attach hub commands and give each command its own row\n    \n    A hub recommendation now carries the slash command of its single routed\n    mode, taken from a table generated from the hubs' own mode registries.\n    A deep-loop command is attached only when the prompt asks for that\n    effort, and a hub stays silent when the command's own row already ranks\n    in the same result. Every /speckit command and /prompt:improve has its\n    own advisor row that passes only on its own phrase or slash string, and\n    a command row and its owner skill no longer count as an ambiguous tie.\n    \n    The umbrella ids command-spec-kit, memory:save, command-memory-save and\n    command-prompt-improver are retired for one id per command. Gold lines,\n    fixtures, both baselines and the Python scorer are re-pointed, and\n    AGENTS.md Gate 4, the root README, the orchestrate agent with its\n    runtime mirrors and the doctor manifest name the deep-loop command rows\n    in their place.\n    \n    The hook asks for the compiled route of the top recommendation only,\n    through the new compiledRouteTopOnly option. /create:changelog now asks\n    first because its release path pushes a tag and publishes a release.\n    Standalone skills may carry command-metadata.json.\n    \n    Component changelog entries, READMEs, the feature catalog, one playbook\n    scenario and the v4.0.2.1 release notes describe the change. Phase 003\n    stays In Progress: plain-chat holdout reach is still 0 of 44.\n    \n    Spec: system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/003-plain-chat-command-reach\n    Commit-Id: 0013668\n\ndiff --git a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/scoring-compatibility.json b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/scoring-compatibility.json\nindex 7bc5f183ca..7319e4ee7c 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/scoring-compatibility.json\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/scoring-compatibility.json\n@@ -1,73 +1,6 @@\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && git -c core.fsmonitor=false log -p -3 -- .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/scoring-compatibility.json | head -160\"}"},"time":{"start":1794535057054,"end":1794535057732}}}}
